Z||000009||StuGood||09-29-2000||07:20 AM||||So Neons are fairly quick little cars, and they can beat Fieros.  Good for them!  Now "everybody" is laughing at us.  So what?  Learn to live with it.<P>Personally, I like sleepers.  But I just don't care for Neons.  On paper, they look pretty good (the numbers, anyway).  But they don't look cool like Fieros do - and never will no matter how fast they go, IMHO.<P>Do I want a cool-looking car, or do I want a quick/fast one?  I'm not picky - I want <B>both</B>!  Oh, and it has to get good mileage... and be durable, quiet & comfortable on long trips, fun to drive, and be reasonably easy to maintain.  The numbers don't show this, and neither does a drag race.   <P>I've lived with people telling me about what poorly-built, unsafe cars my Fieros are, for years. My usual response is to smile and say, "Fine."  Try it sometime. They'll come around eventually.       <P><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-29-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000010||My7Fieros||09-29-2000||07:46 AM||||I better go outside and take a look at my Fieros! Apparently Ive got some sort of super duper stock Fieros, because theres not a single cheap ass Neon (  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ) that has EVER come close to beeting me. Im still scratching my head on this one. And please dont go reading specs on 1/4 mile times on a freekin' Dodge Neon because I dont care...Ive beaten them before, with very little problem. I dont even waste my time on them anymore...<BR>Man, Im in awe...wtf?<P><BR>A Neon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> puh-leez||||reg||5
