Z||000016||Will||09-29-2000||04:38 PM||||P-Man:<BR>     There are three kinds of jobs: good, cheap, and quick. You can have any two: a good job cheap won't be quick, a good job quick won't be cheap, and a cheap job quick won't be good.<BR>     No engine swap is easy. If you want to do it yourself, you must be prepared to spend time learning what to do and how to do it, and a lot of time on top of that actually doing it. For starters, buy a shop manual for your car AND for the donor CAR, not just the donor engine. The shop manual has the wiring diagrams and color codes you need to make your own wiring harness, which is the hardest part fo the swap.<BR>     I don't know anything about your mechanical skills, but if you don't know which end of a wrench to use, an engine swap is a bad place to start.<BR>     I'd help, but I don't know much about 3800's. I imagine that if you asked nicely, someone here could help you, but you must be polite and you must be patient. You must also ask specific questions. If someone posted "How do I put a Northstar into my car?" I would not be very inclined to respond. If someone posted "How do I modify a V6 flywheel for a Northstar?" I would be much more inclined to answer.<BR>     Chris West offers tech support and sells parts because that's his BUSINESS. People here are giving up some of their free time to help you. Just remember that.<BR>     <P>P.S. If you want straight line numbers, look here: <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/math.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/math.htm</A> <P>It has a Java based calculator to ESTIMATE 1/4 mile time/speed.<P>Through intelligent and well-thought out modifications, the Fiero can be made to handle as well as you want it too, but you have to do research about suspension in general.<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 09-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Will||09-29-2000||04:41 PM||||SaleenFiero:<BR>     A heavily modded stock transmission (automatic)would do it, or a somewhat less beefed up 4T65E, or a stock to slightly modded 4T80E.<BR>     One thing I've thought would be interesting would be to do a GN type High-Po build on a FWD 3.8 block and put it in a Fiero with about 20 Psi of boost. Can you say Straight Line Rocket?<BR>||||reg||1
